<title>USA: Hurco Cos Inc Q2 April 30 full results.</title>
<headline>Hurco Cos Inc Q2 April 30 full results.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per-share data, unaudited)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					   April 30,	   April 30,</p>
<p>				     1997	  1996    1997    1996</p>
<p> Sales and service fees    $22,581    $26,095 $44,859 $49,319</p>
<p> Cost of sales and service  15,720     18,864  31,530  35,613</p>
<p> Gross profit		    6,861	7,231  13,329  13,706</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>   administrative expenses   5,217	5,363  10,263  10,412</p>
<p> Operating income		1,644	1,868   3,066   3,294</p>
<p> License fee income, net     6,032	   --   6,175     293</p>
<p> Interest expense		  538	  789   1,060   1,919</p>
<p> Other expense, net		 39	   15	50	32</p>
<p> Income before income taxes  7,097	1,064   8,131   1,636</p>
<p>Foreign withholding and</p>
<p>   Income tax expense	    896	   33     914	33</p>
<p> Net income			6,201	1,031   7,217   1,603</p>
<p> Earnings per common share     .93	  .19    1.08     .29</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>   shares outstanding	  6,659	5,524   6,669   5,555</p>
<p>NOTE: Q2 and 6-mos earnings include licensing fees of $5.1 million, net of expenses and taxes, on settlement agreement with a defendant in on-going patent litigation brought by IMS Technology Inc unit against manufacturers and end-users of computer numerical controls for machine tools. Proceeds from settlement were used to reduce outstanding borrowings. Excluding licensing fees, Q2 and 6-mos net income increased about 3% and 48% over the corresponding year-ago periods.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
